cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "These are test fixtures. Cite them when you reproduce a verdict; do not cite them as a conformance suite for third-party implementations, which does not exist yet."
title: "UIBC conformance vectors: four packages and a six-row expectation gate"
abstract: >-
  Executable evidence packages for UIBC (Unified Integrity Boundary Check):
  clean, tampered, deleted and keyswap, each with a committed expectation table.
  The gate demonstrates the boundary of unpinned verification - a full forgery,
  re-sealed by another key, verifies against itself and is rejected only when
  the owner's public key is pinned. Verdicts are three-valued (PASS, FAIL and
  the explicit UNKNOWN), and the repository carries a receipt ledger for
  third-party runs.
